  "title": "Escape Sequences",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Course: Learn C Programming"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Escape Sequences"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Suppose, we want to print a string like this:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "c",
      "content": "\"What's there?\", asked John"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Since there are quotation marks in it, we have to use \\\" to indicate \". For example,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "c",
      "content": "1#include <stdio.h>\n2\n3int main() {\n4\n5  char message[] = \"\\\"What's there?\\\", asked John\";\n6\n7  printf(\"%s\", message);\n8\n9  return 0;\n10}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "\"What's there?\", asked John"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, \\\" is called an escape sequence. It allows us to include special characters in strings."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Remember \\n? It is also an escape sequence which is used for newline (next line)."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "c",
      "content": "1#include <stdio.h>\n2\n3int main() {\n4\n5  char message[] = \"Hello\\nHow are you?\\nAll good?\";\n6\n7  printf(\"%s\", message);\n8\n9  return 0;\n10}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Hello\nHow are you?\nAll good?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "As you can see, when \\n is encountered, it's treated as a newline."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Note: When a C compiler encounters a string enclosed inside double quotes, it automatically appends a null character, '\\0' at the end by default."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "It helps to identify the end of the string. For example, the string \"Program\" is interpreted by the compiler as:"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "C compiler automatically appends a null character, '\\0' at the end.",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
